# Smart Closet AI 👗

I built this project because I was tired of staring at my wardrobe every morning thinking "I have nothing to wear" — so I made an AI that decides for me!

## What is this?

Smart Closet AI is a full stack web app that helps you manage your wardrobe and get outfit recommendations based on your mood, weather, and occasion. It uses real AI to suggest outfits — not just random combinations.

## Why I built this

I wanted to build something actually useful, not just another todo app. This project taught me how to connect a React frontend with a Python backend, work with real APIs, and integrate AI into a real product.

## Features

- Upload your clothes with photos
- Auto detects the color of your clothing (no manual input needed)
- Get AI outfit recommendations based on occasion and season
- Weather based suggestions — it checks real weather of your city
- Outfit of the Day — generates a fresh outfit every morning
- Plan outfits on a calendar
- Analytics dashboard — see your wardrobe stats
- Chat with AI stylist — ask any fashion question
- Style profile — AI learns your personal preferences

## Tech Stack

- Frontend — React + Vite
- Backend — FastAPI (Python)
- Database — SQLite
- AI — Groq API (Llama 3.1)
- Color Detection — ColorThief + PIL
- Weather — Open-Meteo API (free, no key needed)

## How to run locally

### Backend
```bash
cd backend
pip install fastapi uvicorn python-dotenv groq colorthief pillow requests python-multipart
uvicorn main:app --reload
```

Create a `.env` file in backend folder:
GROQ_API_KEY=your_key_here
Get free key at console.groq.com

### Frontend
```bash
cd frontend
npm install
npm run dev
```

Open http://localhost:5173

